# Handbook sync adapter

This adapter keeps `handbook/` (the bilingual derived documentation system)
consistent with the tree. It adds no workflow, axiom, or status semantics; the
policy is owned by `handbook/_meta/sync-policy.md` and canonical governance
sources always win over handbook content.

1. Before finishing any change under `crates/`, `apps/`, `packages/`, `specs/`,
   `conformance/`, `tests/`, `tools/`, `deploy/`, `.github/`, or root manifests,
   match the changed paths against `handbook/_meta/source-map.json` and update
   the mapped handbook documents in the same formal task and PR.
2. User-visible behavior changes (CLI verbs/flags, configuration files, errors,
   security boundaries, installation, recovery) must update both locales of the
   affected `handbook/*/user/**` and `handbook/*/reference/**` pages.
3. Architecture, data, protocol, authority, or test-environment changes must
   update the affected `handbook/*/developer/**` and `handbook/*/ai/**` pages.
4. Pages with `generated: true` are refreshed only by running
   `node tools/src/generate-handbook.mjs`; never hand-edit them. After editing a
   hand-written page or its mapped sources, run
   `node tools/src/fill-handbook-fingerprints.mjs`.
5. A new tracked file must be classified in
   `handbook/_meta/source-coverage.json` (owning docs, or an excluded category
   with a reason).
6. If a change truly affects no documentation, acknowledge it explicitly:
   pass `DOCS_IMPACT_NONE="<concrete reason>"` to the docs-sync gate and record
   the same reason in the commit/PR description. Blank or trivial reasons do
   not pass.
7. Timing is mandatory, not advisory: the docs-sync gate
   (`node tools/src/docs-sync-gate.mjs --staged|--push`) runs before **every
   commit and push** — enable the repo hooks once per clone with
   `pnpm run hooks:install`. Before flipping a task PR to ready, additionally
   run `node tools/src/check-handbook.mjs`,
   `node tools/src/generate-handbook.mjs --check`, and
   `pnpm run check:consistency`; CI enforces the same set on every PR.
8. When a canonical source (governance, formal plan, `specs/`, `conformance/`,
   standards) conflicts with a handbook page, the canonical source wins; correct
   the handbook page in the same delivery. Never copy dynamic
   `PROGRESS.md`/Gate status into the handbook — link it.
